<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0114/tu_0004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Shared decision-making is a process by which patients and clinicians work together to make optimal health care decisions from medically reasonable options that align with what matters most to patients. Shared decision-making requires: unbiased medical evidence about the risks, benefits, and burdens of each alternative, including no intervention; clinician expertise in communication and tailoring that evidence for individual patients; and patient goals and informed preferences.12" .
