<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/decisions%20about%20the%20location%20of%20death%2C%20home%20services%2C%20and%20hospice%20care> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasSourceMention> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0114/e_0015> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/their%20loved%20ones> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "their loved ones" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/Shared%20decision-making> <http://digistrucmed.org/name> "Shared decision-making" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/RouteEntity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Route Entity" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0114/tu_0003> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Management of patients with HF as their disease becomes end-stage and death seems near includes decisions about when to discontinue treatments designed primarily to prolong life (eg, ICD, hospitalization, tube feeding), decisions on when to initiate treatments to reduce pain and suffering that may hasten death (eg, narcotics), and decisions about the location of death, home services, and hospice care. Exploring patients\\' expressed preferences, values, needs, concerns, means and desires through clinician-led discussion can clarify values-treatment concordance and improve medical decision-making.12" .
